# Per-run Algorithm ISAs. Matches the live ~/.claude convention, where
# LIFEOS/MEMORY/WORK/ is ignored: an ISA is the system of record for ONE run,
# written to disk and never committed. Three complete ISAs sat untracked here
# for weeks reading as uncommitted work. Consequence worth knowing: an ISA is
# NOT recoverable from git history, so anything durable belongs in the commit
# message or in MEMORY/, not only in the ISA.
MEMORY/WORK/

